    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "In response to the manager's request for a proper system to store customer details, you can start by creating a table in SQL to organize customer information properly."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The startup needs to store the following customer details:"
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet_list",
      "items": [
        "First name",
        "Last name",
        "Age",
        "Country"
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "For this, let's create a table with the necessary columns: first_name, last_name, age, and country:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "sql",
      "content": "1CREATE TABLE Customers (\n2    id int,\n3    first_name VARCHAR(50),\n4    last_name VARCHAR(50),\n5    age int,\n6    country VARCHAR(50)\n7);"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "After running the above query, you will see the Customers table in the Available Tables section."
    },
